WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.880
People have been noshing on shrimp since the
beginning of time, but it hasn't always been

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:05.960
an easy catch.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:08.970
Wild stocks declined in the 20th century.

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.540
Shrimp farms emerged to supply what nature
couldn't.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:17.510
Factories processed the harvest, ensuring an
abundance of ready to eat shrimp for the

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:26.050
freezer. Jumbo shrimp have long been big on
the cocktail circuit.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:30.170
Today it comes prepped and frozen, complete
with cocktail sauce.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.930
Just unwrap and thaw.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:38.370
Shrimp cocktail is one of many ready to eat
dishes prepared at this factory in Thailand.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.660
Fresh from the farm, the shrimp undergoes a
quick cold water rinse.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.330
It then rides a perforated conveyor.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:50.950
Rinse water drains through the holes in the
conveyor to keep the shrimp from becoming

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.560
soggy. Still cool.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:59.290
From the icy bath, the curly crustaceans
spill off the conveyor into plastic baskets.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.360
They weigh each basket and then transfer the
shrimp to a larger tub.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.550
To keep the chill on.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.980
They add crushed ice between loads.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:18.600
A temperature of ten degrees Celsius or less
must be maintained throughout.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.880
Processing or quality will suffer.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.340
It's now time for the inevitable, the
heading.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.870
Using a metal tool that's like an open
thimble.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.160
Workers pull the heads off the shrimp with a
few quick tugs.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.150
The heading line is a long and busy one.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.390
The headless shrimp.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:48.550
Now travel to sizing rollers.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:53.840
The space between the rollers is narrow at
first and wider further down.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:59.900
As the rollers spin, smaller shrimp fall
through first and the larger ones continue on

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.430
to fall through further down.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.060
They accumulate in different piles on
conveyors below.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.790
This separates the shrimp into five size
categories.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:10.400
Out of the sorter.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:14.790
An employee samples the shrimp's temperature
to confirm that it remains adequately

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:20.480
chilled. D headed and sorted by size.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:23.480
These shrimp are now ready to come out of
their shells.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.480
On the shelling line.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.400
Some workers cut the tails off and others
leave them on because there's a market for

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:36.840
both. After they peel away the shell, they
cut out the digestive tract that runs along

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.220
the back. It's often referred to as the vein
because it looks like one.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.110
Workers on this line.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.400
Peel and devein.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.960
800 shrimp an hour.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.080
The shrimp then goes to different prep
zones.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:56.220
At this one, an employee dips tail on shrimp
into an egg mixture and then dredges them in

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:01.760
rice flour. He sends them down the line to
the next worker.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.720
Heroes. The flowered shrimp in net rice
paper.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.380
As you can see.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.210
There's a bit of a trick to this.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:20.570
He moistens the edges of the rice paper to
seal the wrap.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:26.300
The result is a spring roll appetizer that
can be frozen until it's ready to be cooked

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:34.520
and served. In another area, a worker
prepares a breaded recipe, again using shrimp

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.200
with the tails still on.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:41.690
This is finger food and with the tails on,
the shrimp will be easier to grip.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.780
He soaks it in seasonings and coats it in
breadcrumbs.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:49.370
Then he dips it in egg batter and breads it
again.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:55.190
The second coating of crumbs will give the
shrimp extra crunch when fried.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.580
The tray is now full.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:59.470
And so it's over to the fry belt.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.360
After a quick trip through hot oil.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.880
The breaded shrimp is perfectly fried.

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:16.610
All the shrimp, including this raw product,
Take a blustery ride through a freezer.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.340
Spread evenly across the conveyor.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:23.150
They freeze individually rather than in big,
icy clumps.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.690
So you don't have to thaw a whole bunch to
get a few shrimp.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:31.790
The frozen shrimp falls into waste stations
at the correct amount.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.890
The bottom opens to release them.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.740
An ice glaze will protect them from freezer
burn.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:41.300
These frozen shrimp products are ready to
leave the factory.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:44.820
From the freezer to the oven to your taste
buds.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.880
With all the prep work done at the factory,
these frozen shrimp products are quite a

00:04:50.880 --> 00:05:00.820
treat. Rice is

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:05.650
an integral part of the Asian diet, so it's
not surprising to find special storage

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:07.760
vessels for it in Thailand.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:13.540
The traditional container is a rice box, a
covered jar handwoven from bamboo and often

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.920
beautifully decorated.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:18.340
They're also produced as decorative items
for export.

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:26.730
Thai rice boxes started out as ordinary
household containers for cooked sticky rice.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.680
Today, they're sought after handicrafts
produced in a range of sizes for storage of

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.320
all kinds or simply for decoration.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.650
Each box is handcrafted from start to
finish.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.920
The artisan begins with thin strips of
bamboo.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:47.220
He splits the strips with his fingernail to
make them the width required for the box size

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:52.940
he's weaving. He lines up the first few
strips on the floor and holds them steady

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:58.580
with his foot as he weaves strips crosswise
through them in a under one over two

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:08.470
sequence. He continues weaving this pattern
until he produces a square that's large

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.570
enough to form the base of the box.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.320
He sprays the base with water to soften up
the bamboo.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:22.170
This prevents the strips from breaking when
he now bends them upward to begin weaving the

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:23.430
sides of the box.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:33.440
Once he's completed the sides, he begins
weaving the boxes neck, pulling the strips

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.720
laterally in a circular direction.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:40.340
He alternates folding one strip upward, one
strip downward.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:47.030
He trims the downward strips, then inserts
the ends through the woven sides.

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:54.680
Next, pulling the strips through the middle.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:07:00.050
He fits a bamboo ring over the outside of
the neck, then another along the inside of

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:03.740
the neck, locking the remaining upward
strips in between.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:09.860
This immobilizes the strips eliminating any
need for nails or glue.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:14.720
It also adds rigidity, reinforcing the next
round shape.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.800
A quick trim of the remaining strips and the
box is fully constructed.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:32.160
He then makes a lid using the same materials
and technique.

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:40.080
Next, artisans coat the outside of the box
and lid with a mixture of chalk, glue and

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:45.840
sawdust. They let the coating dry in the sun
for a day or two until the surface becomes

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.850
hard and smooth like clay.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:52.290
Now an artist gets to work.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.520
First applying two base coats of acrylic
paint.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:08.760
Once the base coats are dry, she places the
box on a turntable and applies a coat of the

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:09.870
background color.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.960
Once that dries, she begins outlining the
design.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.840
Then she fills in the design.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:42.850
Once that's dry, the fine details.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:46.000
It's here that you see the artistry emerge.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:09:01.450
Once the artwork has dried, they encircle
the neck with a band of rattan, then with

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.850
strips of rattan, tie the box to a wooden
stand.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:17.870
At the base of each corner, they weave the
rattan strips into a decorative pattern.

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:34.850
Not only is the rice box entirely handmade,
the artisans never use templates, never take

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:38.210
measurements. They do it all by eye.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:44.660
The inside of the box remains bare.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:49.310
The idea is to see the bamboo and how
skillfully it's woven.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:55.560
It's a natural, non-toxic surface against
which it's safe to store rice.

